        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "What is Canvas UGC?", a: "Canvas UGC is a delivery model where brands pay creators to post content on brand-owned social accounts. The brand's account is the 'canvas.' Creators are paid per view (CPM $2-$6) or through a hybrid model (base pay + view bonuses). The brand retains the account, the audience, and the content library." },
          { q: "How is Canvas UGC different from Tech UGC?", a: "Canvas UGC describes the delivery model — where content is posted (brand accounts) and how creators are paid (per view). Tech UGC describes the content category — creator-made video about software, apps, and AI tools. They often overlap but are separate concepts. A lifestyle brand can run Canvas UGC. A tech brand can buy Tech UGC content without using brand accounts." },
          { q: "How many creators do I need?", a: "A single-account Canvas UGC program typically needs 10+ active creators to maintain the recommended volume of 15-40 videos per month. Multi-account programs require proportionally more. OKAD handles creator recruitment from our network." },
          { q: "How long does warmup take?", a: "Typically 1-3 weeks of active niche engagement and initial posting before the algorithm starts distributing content meaningfully. Skipping warmup is the most common mistake — accounts that immediately flood content without warmup see minimal organic reach." },
          { q: "What platforms work for Canvas UGC?", a: "Primarily TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, and Facebook Reels. TikTok is typically the highest-volume channel due to its content discovery algorithm." },
          { q: "How much do creators earn?", a: "With CPM rates of $2-$6, active creators working across multiple brand accounts earn $3K-$15K+ per month. Earnings scale with volume and quality. The model rewards consistency — aggregate volume across many posts, not chasing individual viral hits." },
          { q: "Can organic Canvas UGC posts become paid ads?", a: "Yes, and this is one of the model's biggest advantages. Top organic performers can be promoted directly via Spark Ads (TikTok), Partnership Ads (Meta), or YouTube Shorts Promote. Organic performance serves as a free testing signal for what works in paid." },
